"5551","méid","amount / quanity / extent / number
<small>an méid airgid = the amount of money</small>
<small>an méid daoine = the amount of people</small>
<small>an méid ama a thógann sé = the amount of time it takes</small>
<small>ó thaobh méid agus caighdeáin = in terms of quantity and quality</small>
<li>an méid seo = this much
<small>tá an méid seo cinnte = this much is certain</small>
<small>is fíor an méid sin = that much is true</small>
<small>tabharfaidh mé an méid sin dó = I'll give him that much</small>
<li>size/magnitude
<small>tá siad ar aon mhéid = they are the same size</small>
<small>an bhfuil an mhéid cheart ann? = is it the right size (e.g. clothes)</small>
<small>crith talún ar mhéid 8.1 = a quake of 8.1 magnitude</small>
<aside>takes the genitive, either singular (airgid, ama) or plural (daoine)</aside>
<aside>for questions, <b>cén mhéid</b> means 'what size', e.g. 'cén mhéid tú?' = 'what size do you wear?'
but for the question 'how much', the dictionary spelling changes to 'méad': 'cé mhéad?' = 'how much?', although pronounciation is probably still 'cé mhéid'</aside>","méid",90,"Noun","Noun","nf","an méid sin",0,0,0,NA,"","",0,FALSE,NA
