"835","beirt","two persons
<aside>takes plural (unlike e.g. dhá rud = two things), and lenites as it's a feminine noun:
<br>beirt chailíní = two girls
<br>beirt phaistí = two children
</aside>
<aside>
this is a genitive plural  (a pair <b>of</b>...), which can be different to the regular plural:
<br>men = fir -> beirt fhear = two men
<br>women = mná -> beirt bhan = two women
<br>sons = mic -> beirt mhac = two sons
<a href=""https://blogs.transparent.com/irish/na-huimhreacha-pearsanta-ar-leanuint/"">more info</a> on this including why 'beirt' (and not 'triúr' etc.) causes lenition.
</aside>","beirt",139,"Noun","Noun","nf2","<div class=""nf d2"">an b<i>h</i>e<i>irt</i>/na beirte<em>anna</em><div class=""decl"">n<i>f</i>2 strong plural</div><i>na</i> beirte/na mbeirte<em>anna</em></div>",0,0,0,NA,"","",0,FALSE,NA
