"8459","triúr","three people
<aside>causes genitive plural in succeeding noun (a trio <b>of</b>...): 
<br>triúr fear = three men (men = fir)
<br>triúr ban = three women (women = mná)
<br>triúr mac = three sons (sons = mic)
The following have strong plurals (no change in genitive plural), so the genitive is invisible:
<br>triúr deartháireacha = three brothers
<br>triúr deirfúiracha = three sisters
<br>triúr iníonacha = three daughters
</aside>","triúr",546,"Noun","Noun","nm1","<div class=""nm d1"">an tri<i>úr</i>/na triúir<div class=""decl"">n<i>m</i>1 weak plural</div><i class=""weak"">an</i> triúir/na dtriúr</div>",0,0,0,NA,"","",0,FALSE,NA
