"1571","ceathrar","four people
<aside>causes genitive plural in succeeding noun (a quartet <b>of</b>...): 
<br>ceathrar fear = four men (men = fir)
<br>ceathrar ban = four women (women = mná)
<br>ceathrar mac = four sons (sons = mic)
The following have strong plurals (no change in genitive plural), so the genitive is invisible:
<br>ceathrar deartháireacha = four brothers
<br>ceathrar deirfúiracha = four sisters
<br>ceathrar iníonacha = four daughters
<br>ceathrar páistí = four children
</aside>","ceathrar",1085,"Noun Adjective & Pronoun","Noun","nm1","<div class=""nm d1"">an ceathrar/na ceathrair<div class=""decl"">n<i>m</i>1 weak plural</div><i class=""weak"">an</i> c<i>h</i>eathrair/na gceathrar</div>",0,0,0,NA,"","",0,FALSE,NA
