"6010","ochtar","eight people
<aside>causes genitive plural in the succeeding noun
<br>for 'strong plural' nouns, this is the same as the regular plural:
<br>ochtar páistí = eight children
<br>ochtar dochtúirí = eight doctors
<br>ochtar iníonacha = eight daughters
<br>but certain nouns have a separate genitive plural: 
<br>ochtar fear = eight men ('fir' is the normal plural)
<br>ochtar ban = eight women ('mná is the normal plural)
<br>ochtar mac = eight sons ('mic' is the normal plural)
</aside>","ochtar",3024,"Noun","Noun","nm1","<div class=""nm d1"">an <i>t</i>-ochtar/na hochtair<div class=""decl"">n<i>m</i>1 weak plural</div><i class=""weak"">an</i> ochtair/na n-ochtar</div>",0,0,0,NA,"","",0,FALSE,NA
