"1400","cár","where (did)
<aside>'cár' is really a form of 'cá' used with past tense of regular verbs<br>
cár fhág tú iad = where did you leave them (regular)
<br>
cá bhfuair tú iad = where did you get them (irregular)
</aside>
<aside>
it's also used with the copula to mean 'what' in the past tense:
<small>cár locht orm é? What fault was it in me?</small>
</aside>
<aside>
also nm1 'grin / grimace - showing teeth' and used in Donegal in place of 'fiacla'
<small>nigh do chár = brush your teeth</small>
</aside>","cár",3212,"Interrogative","Noun","","",0,0,0,NA,"","",0,FALSE,NA
