"5872","naonúr","nine people
<aside>causes genitive plural in the succeeding noun 
<br>for 'strong plural' nouns, this is the same as the regular plural:
<br>naonúr páistí = nine children 
<br>naonúr dochtúirí = nine doctors 
<br>naonúr iníonacha = nine daughters 
<br>but certain nouns have a separate genitive plural:
<br>naonúr fear = nine men ('fir' is the normal plural) 
<br>naonúr ban = nine women ('mná is the normal plural) 
<br>naonúr mac = nine sons ('mic' is the normal plural)
</aside>","naonúr",3603,"Noun","Noun","nm1","<div class=""nm d1"">an naon<i>úr</i>/na naonúir<div class=""decl"">n<i>m</i>1 weak plural</div><i class=""weak"">an</i> naonúir/na naonúr</div>",0,0,0,NA,"","",0,FALSE,NA
