"7139","sea","contraction of 'is ea' (it is)
<aside>means 'yes' when given as the answer to an indefinite copular question, e.g. 'an dochtúir í Síle?' (is Sheila a doctor?) &mdash; 'sea' (yes/she is) nó 'ní hea' (no/she is not)</aside>
<aside>if the question is definite 'an é Síle an dochtúir?' (is Seile the doctor), the affirmative is 'is í', which can be shortened to 'sí</aside>
<aside>sometimes (grammatically incorrectly) used as a general purpose 'yes'; the correct way of saying yes or no is to echo the verb, e.g. 'ar bhris tú an fhuinneog?' &mdash; 'bhris' nó 'níor bhris'</aside>","is",3731,"Copular Affirmative","Copula","","",0,0,0,NA,"","",0,FALSE,NA
"7140","sea","contraction of 'is ea' (it is)
