"3018","dóbair","almost
<small>dóbair dom titim / dóbair gur thit mé = I almost fell</small>
<li>it nearly happened (that)
<small>ba dhóbair go bhfuair mé é = I almost got it</small>
<small>ba dhóbair nár dhoirt mé é = I nearly spilled it</small>
<small>chuaigh sé go dtí an dóbair = it was touch and go</small>
<aside>can be used with either a positive or a negative to have the same meaning of 'almost'</aside>
<aside>'dóbair' is slightly more prevalent in Ulster Irish. An alternative structure with the same meaning is 'is beag nár' or 'ní mor nár'</aside>
<aside>further emphasis can be added as follows <b>ba ródhóbair dom titim</b> = I <i>very</i> nearly fell</aside>","dóbair",6147,"","Noun","","dóbair go
