"873","bíodh","be (as imperative)
<small>bíodh ciall agat = have sense</small>
<small>bíodh deoch agat! = have a drink!</small>
<small>bíodh lá maith agaibh = have a good day (y'all)</small>
<small>ná bíodh fearg ort = don’t be angry</small>
<li>so be it = bíodh amhlaidh
<li>if it were
<small>bíodh agus go bhfaca tú é = granted that you saw him</small>
<aside>
<b>bíodh</b> is actually the 3rd person imperative, but is combined with <b>agat</b>/<b>agaibh</b>/<b>ort</b> in the examples above to address a person (or persons) directly. 
Use <b>bí</b> or <b>bígí</b> for direct imperatives:
<small>bí i do shuí = be seated</small>
<small>bígí reidh! = (y'all) be ready</small>
</aside> ","bí",6578,"Third Person Imperative of 'bí'","Verb","","",0,0,0,NA,"","",0,FALSE,NA
